      "ImageDescription": {
        "value": "A special 'bath' to detect frogs infected with the chytrid fungus - one of the worst killers of frogs - has been concocted by CSIRO researchers. The bath consists of modified pond water, allowing researchers to collect the fungus zoospores  in the water.  Pictured here, a  Great barred frog (Mixophyes balbus) takes the 'bath' to determine if it is infected with the chytrid fungus. Photographer: Frank Filippi, 2002.",
        "source": "commons-desc-page"
